WEBVTT

00:00:00.103 --> 00:00:05.706
This practice is about explanation not only
execution Run

00:00:05.733 --> 00:00:10.088
the multiplication query again and focus on one
patient with multiple admissions

00:00:10.325 --> 00:00:16.082
lab results and prescriptions Your task is to
explain why joined rows

00:00:16.108 --> 00:00:21.903
is larger than each underlying event count A strong
explanation would mention

00:00:21.916 --> 00:00:27.208
combinations For one patient each admission can
combine with each lab result

00:00:27.235 --> 00:00:31.103
and each prescription because all three detail
tables are joined independently through

00:00:31.129 --> 00:00:36.777
patient ID After you understand the multiplication
compare this

00:00:36.804 --> 00:00:42.399
result with the pre-aggregation pattern from the
earlier slide Do not try

00:00:42.426 --> 00:00:47.626
to memorize a rule such as always use DISTINCT
Instead identify the

00:00:47.652 --> 00:00:53.257
target grain and the cardinality of every
relationship When several one-to-many tables

00:00:53.284 --> 00:00:56.573
are joined to the same parent multiplication should
be one of the

00:00:56.586 --> 00:00:57.731
first things you check
